-- title:
--   Weight at most p+1 for a twisted mod-p Hecke eigensystem
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta_W \neq 0$ whose mod-$p$ representation is irreducible in the sense of [`WeierstrassCurve.ModRepIsIrreducible`](def/FLTPrelim_ModularRep.html#L94): after base change of $W$ along $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Q}$, the $p$-torsion submodule of the group of points over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is nontrivial and its only Galois-stable $\mathbb{Z}/p$-submodules are $\bot$ and $\top$. Let $N' \geq 1$ with $p \nmid N'$, and assume that if $p = 3$ then $N'$ has a prime factor $q$ with $q \equiv 2 \pmod 3$. Let $S_0$ be a finite set of natural numbers with $p \in S_0$, let $k \geq 2$ be an integer and $i$ a natural number. Here `heckeAlgebra N' k S₀` is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_k(\Gamma_0(N'))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N'$ with $\ell \notin S_0$ together with the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N'$ with $q \notin S_0$, and $a_\ell(W) = \ell + 1 - \#W(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)$ is the trace of Frobenius of the reduction of $W$ modulo $\ell$, where $\ell$ is called a good prime for $W$ when $\ell \nmid \Delta_W$. Suppose $\mathfrak{m}_k$ is a maximal ideal of `heckeAlgebra N' k S₀` containing $p$ and containing $T_\ell - \ell^i a_\ell(W)$ for every prime $\ell \notin S_0$ with $\ell \nmid N'$ and $\ell \nmid \Delta_W$. Then there are an integer $k'$ with $2 \leq k' \leq p + 1$, a natural number $j$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}'$ of `heckeAlgebra N' k' S₀` containing $p$ and containing $T_\ell - \ell^j a_\ell(W)$ for all such primes $\ell$.
--
--   This is the weight part of Serre's conjecture in Edixhoven's form — the weight may be taken at most $p+1$ after a cyclotomic twist, with the level $N'$ unchanged — stated for a Hecke eigensystem that is a twist of the one attached to an elliptic curve over $\mathbb{Q}$, and recorded as a statement about maximal ideals of the Hecke algebra with residue characteristic $p$. It feeds the normalisation of weights in the modularity argument, and is used by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_weight_le_succ_pow_mul_apOfModel_of_exists_prime_dvd_mod_three_eq_two`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_weight_le_succ_pow_mul_apOfModel_of_exists_prime_dvd_mod_three_eq_two).
